{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1853 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6a7066aa97f6a59e9cd7e6ca06021e69a7720f5c122f7adface743bd227037ae" :edb/db-before-t 1852 :edb/db-after-t 1853 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535165 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:26:02.378Z" 13194139535165 true] [17592186129204 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334893 13194139535165 true] [17592186129204 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334900 13194139535165 true] [17592186129205 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334907 13194139535165 true] [17592186129205 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334914 13194139535165 true] [17592186129664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535165 true] [17592186129664 1100 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +v\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=v\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=w.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $\\theta $ is a fixed constant." 13194139535165 true] [17592186129664 1100 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$x = u\\cos θ + v\\sin θ, y = v\\cos θ - u\\sin θ, z = w$.\nYou may assume that $θ$ is a fixed constant." 13194139535165 false] [17592186129664 1145 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334894 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1089 "q-161804" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1100 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} \\\\ {e}^{x+y} \\\\ {e}^{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1113 #uuid "cd9b866e-9272-50ff-85b4-6c1084f92b4b" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334893 1145 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nu(x,y,z)={e}^{x},\\,v(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y},\\,w(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y+z}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & ={e}^{x} & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & ={e}^{x+y} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & ={e}^{x+y} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & ={e}^{x+y+z} & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & ={e}^{x+y+z} & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & ={e}^{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & 0 & 0 \\\\ {e}^{x+y} & {e}^{x+y} & 0 \\\\ {e}^{x+y+z} & {e}^{x+y+z} & {e}^{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{x}|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y} & 0 \\\\ {e}^{x+y+z} & {e}^{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({e}^{2x+2y+z}-0) \\\\  & ={e}^{3x+2y+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting down $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}$ in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x+2y+z} & ={e}^{x+(x+y)+(x+y+z)} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x+y}\\cdot {e}^{x+y+z} \\\\  & =uvw\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uvw}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334895 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334896 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334897 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334898 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334899 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1041 "selection" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334896 13194139535165 true] [17592186334894 1110 #uuid "63b7a310-ade4-58e8-b4ea-654edb7d197b" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334895 1034 "\\frac{1}{u+v+w}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334895 1111 #uuid "5fc67b92-7e58-5e36-a52d-8e7f608415ae" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334896 1034 "\\frac{1}{uvw}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334896 1111 #uuid "9818f4b3-85fa-52d0-8709-84e374fb31cf" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334897 1034 "{e}^{u+v+w}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334897 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334897 1111 #uuid "2010a482-5418-5892-b632-2565f4efce2f" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334898 1034 "{e}^{uvw}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334898 1111 #uuid "a332cfa6-4564-5891-9e36-c54f18a901b2" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334899 1034 "u+v+w" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334899 1111 #uuid "81c78410-b478-59e9-a529-82f6ae13fa7d" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334901 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1089 "q-161807" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1100 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y{z}^{2} \\\\ z{x}^{2} \\\\ x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$\n\n*Hint: You can assume that $x,y,z\\ne 0.$*" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1113 #uuid "38c44dcf-6520-59f3-8029-220189570126" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334900 1145 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nu(x,y,z)=y{z}^{2},\\,v(x,y,z)=z{x}^{2},\\,w(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & ={z}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =2yz \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =2xz & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & ={y}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =2xy & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & {z}^{2} & 2yz \\\\ 2xz & 0 & {x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & 2xy & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-{z}^{2}|\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & 0\\end{aligned}|+2yz|\\begin{aligned}2xz & 0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & 2xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-{z}^{2}(0-{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+2yz(4{x}^{2}yz-0) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2} \\\\  & =9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting down $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}$ in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2} & =9{({x}^{3}{y}^{3}{z}^{3})}^{2/3} \\\\  & =9{(y{z}^{2}\\cdot z{x}^{2}\\cdot x{y}^{2})}^{2/3} \\\\  & =9(uvw)^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9(uvw)^{2/3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334902 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334903 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334904 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334905 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334906 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1041 "selection" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334904 13194139535165 true] [17592186334901 1110 #uuid "35a80d44-28aa-56f7-a62d-2782d5c441df" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334902 1034 "(uvw)^{2/3}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334902 1111 #uuid "f49f37eb-8c65-5f95-8b28-b892f2a417c6" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334903 1034 "\\frac{9}{(uvw)^{2}}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334903 1111 #uuid "7b68d588-2d07-5f63-9fec-dbfdc741522c" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334904 1034 "\\frac{1}{9(uvw)^{2/3}}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334904 1111 #uuid "4662d8df-b0e0-5ac4-8e6b-85f942141fc7" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334905 1034 "3(uvw)^{1/3}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334905 1111 #uuid "ad722fb6-79f9-5975-bfd5-79ff1d0f10cb" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334906 1034 "3(uvw)^{3}" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535165 true] [17592186334906 1111 #uuid "43d51177-a4ea-5a11-bea8-325d10e67520" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334908 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1089 "q-161814" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+2w \\\\ v-u \\\\ uw\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1113 #uuid "d8752c18-2285-5bd2-a3b2-ba4d0420bd04" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334907 1145 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+2w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v-u,\\,z(u,v,w)=uw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ w & 0 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ w & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(u-0)+2(0-w) \\\\  & =u-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ u-2w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u-2w=0$ defines the plane $u=2w.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334909 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334910 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334911 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334912 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334913 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1041 "selection" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334913 13194139535165 true] [17592186334908 1110 #uuid "eefaf736-c84d-5cb0-bc51-7583585ed117" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334909 1034 "The critical points lie on the plane $u+v-2w=0.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334909 1111 #uuid "8d938565-d343-55fc-9f4e-0c3587252094" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334910 1034 "The critical points lie on the elliptic cylinder ${u}^{2}+2{w}^{2}=1.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334910 1111 #uuid "9980731d-9aae-57af-bb7e-5241e7dbeda4" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334911 1034 "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={u}^{2}.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334911 1111 #uuid "588c9b27-9ad4-55da-b027-8edba3f8d053" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334912 1034 "The critical points lie on the $vw-$ plane." 13194139535165 true] [17592186334912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334912 1111 #uuid "7cba160d-b5b2-5592-9faa-f0cd70db5ad1" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334913 1034 "The critical points lie on the plane $u=2w.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334913 1111 #uuid "7033e3f1-f8a3-50c7-8818-cb8d0cdacd71" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334915 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1089 "q-161815" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{u} \\\\ vw \\\\ u+w\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1113 #uuid "3e159eb2-4d19-5beb-a05c-bcfc839eb278" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334914 1145 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\sqrt{u},\\,y(u,v,w)=vw,\\,z(u,v,w)=u+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & w & v \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}|\\begin{aligned}w & v \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ w & v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}(w-0)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}} & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $w=0$ defines the plane $w=0,$ i.e., $uv$-plane." 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334916 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334917 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334918 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334919 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334920 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1041 "selection" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334920 13194139535165 true] [17592186334915 1110 #uuid "985437c0-012d-5cc2-9af5-d446a5d74765" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334916 1034 "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." 13194139535165 true] [17592186334916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334916 1111 #uuid "3738a9d9-01e2-58cf-8cab-2ab5d72ce73a" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334917 1034 "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=2.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334917 1111 #uuid "be70f332-f341-5e71-94b0-d6bd25b4cec4" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334918 1034 "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={w}^{2}.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334918 1111 #uuid "2f530d4f-cb60-5617-895e-91aa8b2c80f4" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334919 1034 "The critical points lie on the plane $u=w.$" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334919 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535165 true] [17592186334919 1111 #uuid "d9876f17-930f-5840-b932-a41eeec88d04" 13194139535165 true] [17592186334920 1034 "The critical po